b model, run structural relaxation across 20 vacuum layer thickness conditions from 0.5 Å to 10.0 Å in 0.5 Å steps:\n     `[0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0, 3.5, 4.0, 4.5, 5.0, 5.5, 6.0, 6.5, 7.0, 7.5, 8.0, 8.5, 9.0, 9.5, 10.0]`.\n  2. Re-run 5.0 Å and 10.0 Å under the new standardized convergence threshold (`minimize 1.0e-6 1.0e-2 100 150`).\n  3. Use identical DFT and relaxation settings to recent calculations (QE 7.6, `ecutwfc = 40.0 Ry`, `ecutrho = 320.0 Ry`, `conv_thr = 1.0e-5 Ry`, $\\Gamma$-point, `local-TF 0.3`).\n  4. Automatically create dedicated folders on NAS `\\\\192.168.12.69\\Results\\yamazaki\\research\\{101_0}2周期〇Å` (where `〇` is the vacuum thickness value, matching user naming such as `{101_0}2周期0.5Å`, `{101_0}2周期1Å`, `{101_0}2周期1.5Å`, ..., `{101_0}2周期10Å`), and save all calculation data into each respective folder.\n- **Scope & Constraints**:\n  - Do not overwrite existing calculation directories; create `calc_2H-SiC_10-10_2periods_vac<V>A_rtx5080/`.\n  - Maintain strict element mapping: Type 1 = C, Type 2 = Si.\n  - Automatically generate 3 progression graphs (`Total_Energy_progression.*`, `Total_Force_progression.*`, `Total_SCF_Correction_progression.*`) per condition.\n  - Compute surface fracture energy $\\gamma = \\frac{E_{\\text{slab}} - E_{\\text{bulk}}(72)}{2A} \\times 16.021766$ against true bulk $E_{\\text{bulk}}(72) = -31,935.3572\\text{ eV}$ ($2A = 279.497664\\text{ \\AA}^2$, effective denominator = `17.44487243166577`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed Deliverables**:\n  1. Built end-to-end automation sweep script [`run_2periods_vacuum_sweep_0.5_to_10A.py`](file:///home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/run_2periods_vacuum_sweep_0.5_to_10A.py):\n     - Automatically generates natural cleavage slab models via ASE `surface(bulk, indices=(1,0,0), layers=2)` and verifies interlayer spacing profile `[0.8881, 1.7758, 0.8881]`.\n     - Runs MDI relaxation with LAMMPS (`lmp`) + QE engine (`qe_mdi_engine_rtx